implementationPlan.description:
RED FIRST (sh harness only). Add a daemon-free, git-free self-restart case to scripts/tests/postflight.sh right after the heartbeat-sidecar checks: after the `fi` that closes the `count_after_wait` check, and before `# --- Quality gate (settings.qualityGate)`. Locate it by those anchors, never by line number: task-84150869 and task-07474ee4 edit this file first.

(1) Shared sequence script. Step 3 writes the SAME bytes into postflight.ps1:
cat > "$TMP_DIR/restart-sequence.cjs" <<'JS'
// Self-restart RPC sequence, byte-identical in postflight.sh and postflight.ps1:
// c = claim_next_task (the daemon re-registers a worker on its claim), r = this
// seat's deregister_worker with reason wrapper_restart, x = any other deregister.
// The last line may still be mid-append, so an unparsable line is skipped.
const fs=require('fs'),[file,worker]=process.argv.slice(2);
const text=fs.existsSync(file)?fs.readFileSync(file,'utf8'):'';
const rows=text.split('\n').flatMap(l=>{try{return [JSON.parse(l)];}catch(e){return [];}});
process.stdout.write(rows.map(r=>r.tool==='claim_next_task'?'c':r.tool!=='deregister_worker'?'':
  r.args&&r.args.workerId===worker&&r.args.reason==='wrapper_restart'?'r':'x').join(''));
JS
The script reads <project>/.moe/evidence-rpcs.jsonl. The fake proxy already logs every claim_next_task and deregister_worker there, in call order, so the fake proxy does NOT change.

(2) Fixture:
- mkdir "$TMP_DIR/self-restart", then cp -R "$ROOT_DIR/scripts" into it. The restart deregisters through the sibling moe-call.sh.
- chmod +x the copied moe-agent.sh: exec needs it.
- Create a project dir with .moe/project.json {"settings":{"autoCommit":false}}, an empty .moe/messages/chan-general.jsonl, and .moe/daemon.json. moe-call.sh refuses to run without daemon.json (scenario W does the same). No git.

(3) Launch the COPY in the background by its absolute path, with the same env shape as the heartbeat case:
PATH="$TMP_DIR:$PATH" HOME="$HOME_DIR" MOE_PROXY_PATH="$FAKE_PROXY" FAKE_CLAIM_MODE=idle MOE_DISABLE_HEARTBEAT=1 <copy> --project <proj> --worker-id worker-self-restart --role worker --no-start-daemon --command /bin/true --loop --poll-interval 1 >"$TMP_DIR/self-restart.out" 2>&1 &
Idle claims launch no CLI, and the loop polls every second. Add the pid to LIVE_PIDS at once, so an abort cannot leak a looping wrapper. Restore LIVE_PIDS after the case kills it: a dead pid can be reused.

(4) Three stages. Each stage has its own deadline of $POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC (measure with $SECONDS) and polls every 0.5 s. EVERY poll fails at once if:
- the sequence contains x (the hand-over went through an exit path);
- its count of r exceeds the changes made so far (a restart with no on-disk change behind it, i.e. thrash);
- kill -0 says the wrapper is gone.
The stages:
 a) wait for ^c;
 b) printf '\n# self-restart probe 1\n' >> <copy>, then wait for ^c+rcc: exactly one restart, a fresh registration, and one more quiet check;
 c) printf '\n# self-restart probe 2\n' >> <copy>, then wait for ^c+rc{2,}rcc.
Only append. The file ends with the main loop's `done`, which the running bash has already parsed, so the old process never reads the new bytes; exec re-reads the whole file. The leading \n keeps the comment on its own line. Keep each regex in a variable for [[ =~ ]].

(5) Snapshot the sequence, then kill -KILL the wrapper and `wait ... || true`. Assert:
- the snapshot matches ^c+rc{2,}rc{2,}$: two restarts for two changes, each followed by a fresh claim, and at least 2 quiet checks after the last;
- self-restart.out has exactly 2 lines 'wrapper source changed on disk; restarting to load it'. Use grep -Fc ... || true, because grep -c exits 1 on zero matches under set -e.

(6) Error handling:
- A failure helper kills the wrapper and prints the output file and .moe/deregister.log to stderr, then one line `SELF-RESTART FAILED: <why> (sequence: <seq>)`, then exits 1.
- Every wait is bounded. An abort under set -e still reaches the harness EXIT trap, which kills LIVE_PIDS.
- Echo '[self-restart] a changed wrapper restarts once per change and re-registers' at the start and '[self-restart] ok' at the end.
- Never print a line starting with SKIP: CI's postflight-safe.mjs fails a run on one.
- Leave SCOPE_SCENARIOS_RUN alone: this case sits outside that counted block.

(7) RED on the REAL wrapper. The case copies the working-tree scripts/, so running it touches nothing live. Build a subset harness by anchors (mem:pattern-postflight-red-proof-via-temp-tree): [0, `FROZEN_SUITE=`) + this case + `echo "PASS postflight.sh"`. Put it in D:/moe-scratch/<unique>/scripts/tests/ beside a scripts/ copy, so ROOT_DIR is the scratch root. Run it against the UNFIXED moe-agent.sh. It must FAIL with 'the wrapper exited', sequence c+r, and the output must show 'Error: Provide --project or --project-name'. That is the argv bug fixed in step 2. Paste the failure lines into the step note.
